## How `.vel` components are written

```html
<template>
  <section class="card">
    <h2>{{ title }}</h2>
    <ul><li v-for="item in items" :key="item.id">{{ item.name | capitalize }}</li></ul>
    <button @click="add">Add</button>
  </section>
</template>

<script>
import Child from "./Child.vel";

export default {
  components: { Child },
  props: { title: String },
  data() { return { items: [] }; },
  computed: { count() { return this.items.length; } },
  created() {},
  mounted() { this.load(); },
  unmounted() {},
  methods: {
    async load() { /* fetch data, then assign this.items */ },
    add() { this.$emit("added"); }
  }
};
</script>

<style scoped>
.card { padding: 1rem; }
</style>
```

- Components are options objects: `data`, `props`, `computed`, `watch`, `methods`, lifecycle hooks, `components`.
- `data()` runs without props. Copy props into local state in `created()` (see known issues).
- Parent to child: props. Child to parent: `this.$emit("name", payload)` and `@name="handler"`.
- Use `:key` on every `v-for`.
- `<style scoped>` does not reach elements that Teloce creates at runtime (for example chart annotations). Put
  those rules in a second, unscoped `<style>` block.
- Shared runtime helpers are imported by package name, like in Node.js:
  `import { http, action, createScope } from "teloce/runtime";`. The build rewrites it to the right relative path.
  Releases before this feature need the relative form (`"../teloce-runtime.js"` from `static/js/`).

## Directives

The complete, authoritative list is `@@DOCS_DIR@@/directives.md`. Do not use a directive that is not documented there.
In this project the ones you will meet most are:

| Need | Use | Read |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lists, conditions, forms, events | `v-for`, `v-if`, `v-model`, `@event`, `:attribute` | `template-syntax.md`, `cheatsheet.md` |
| Scrollytelling | `v-scrolly` on the container, `data-v-step` or `v-step` on each step, `@step` | `lesson-scrollytelling.md` |
| Chart note | `v-chart-annotation="{ text, x, position }"` | `directives.md` |
| Poll an endpoint | `poll="/api/x" interval="5000" poll-target="name"` | `lesson-live-data.md` |
| Element behavior | `use:actionName="params"` | `lesson-use-actions.md` |
| Custom directive | the directive contract | `directive-contracts.md` |

## Network

- `http` for normal JSON requests. Error statuses resolve, so check `res.ok`. Only transport failures throw
  (`error.code` is `timeout`, `aborted` or `network`).
- `action.call("name", data)` calls a named server function. Failures resolve as `{ success: false, error, code }`.
- `createScope()` cancels requests when the component unmounts: call `scope.dispose()` in `unmounted()`.
- Full reference: `@@DOCS_DIR@@/network-api.md`.

## Rules

1. **Never trust the browser.** Validate and clean every payload on the server. The server creates ids and any
   names the client depends on.
2. **Escape output.** `{{ }}` writes text. Do not render user-supplied HTML. See `@@DOCS_DIR@@/security.md`.
3. **Add authentication** before exposing any route or action that changes data. Do not mark actions public
   without a reason.
4. **Keep components small.** Props down, events up. Put shared state in the parent.
5. **Do not edit `dist/`** and do not commit it.
6. **No new dependencies** without asking. Do not add Node tooling.
7. **Match the existing style**: formatting, naming and file layout.

## Known issues, in short

Details and workarounds are in `@@DOCS_DIR@@/known-issues.md`.

- `v-scrolly` may not start when its steps are rendered by `v-for` or arrive with async data (older releases).
- `v-model` on a `<select>` with looped options may not preselect the saved value (older releases).
- Props are not available inside `data()`.
- `in:` and `out:` transitions on a `v-if` element can leave the element on screen in some cases.

## Verify every change

1. Rebuild and run the app.
2. Open the page and check the browser console for errors.
3. Exercise the feature you changed. For backend routes, call them with `curl` and check error cases too.
4. If a test suite exists, run it.
5. Tell the user what you changed, how you checked it, and anything you could not check.
